8.  Is Tomcat Manager an application?

Yes.

The Tomcat Manager is a web application bundled with Tomcat.

Location: /opt/tomcat/webapps/manager

Access URL: http://:8080/manager/html

------------------------------------------------------------------------

9.  Manager vs Host Manager

Manager: - Deploy applications - Start/Stop applications - Reload
applications - View deployed applications

Host Manager: - Create virtual hosts - Delete virtual hosts - Manage
virtual host configuration

------------------------------------------------------------------------

Interview Summary

Tomcat uses role-based access control to secure its management
applications. The manager-gui role provides access to the web-based
Manager application. The manager-script role allows automated
deployments through scripts or Jenkins. The admin-gui role provides
access to the Host Manager for managing virtual hosts. The
RemoteAddrValve is commented out in lab environments to allow remote
access. In production, it is recommended to keep it enabled and allow
only trusted IP addresses.
